#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151883 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b677c92-5390-5cd1-b1d3-b84d180c2b3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "203ff7a1-64cf-5564-8e7c-7ff9f652911a" :question/math-academy-id "e-6559" :question/problem "If $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 + 5\\textrm{i} \\\\ 5 - 9\\textrm{i} \\\\ -7 + 8\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ find $\\,\\overline{\\mathbf{x}}$." :question/worked-solution "To find the complex conjugate of a vector, we take the complex conjugate of the entries of the vector. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx^(―) &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 + 5\\textrm{i} \\\\ 5 - 9\\textrm{i} \\\\ -7 + 8\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}^(―) \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 + 5\\textrm{i}^(―) \\\\ 5 - 9\\textrm{i}^(―) \\\\ -7 + 8\\textrm{i}^(―)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 - 5\\textrm{i} \\\\ 5 + 9\\textrm{i} \\\\ -7 - 8\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151884 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "689f9f44-4776-56a7-915f-d0dab0755002" :knowledge-point/title "Computing Components of the Real and Imaginary Parts of a Complex Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "a2c8f19f-6c69-5891-847e-b6ef26f657bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-6560" :question/problem "If $\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ b\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ d\\end{bmatrix}$ are the real and imaginary parts of the vector $\\begin{bmatrix}-3 + 7\\textrm{i} \\\\ 5 - 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ what is the value of $ab+cd$?" :question/worked-solution "For the given vector $\\begin{bmatrix}-3 + 7\\textrm{i} \\\\ 5 - 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix}$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 + 7\\textrm{i} \\\\ 5 - 2\\textrm{i}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(Re(x)) + \\textrm{i}\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}_(⏟)_(Im(x))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore\n\n$$\na=-3, b=5, c=7\n$$\n\nand $d=-2$, which implies that\n\n$$\nab+cd=(-3) \\cdot 5 + 7 \\cdot (-2) = -29\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186151943 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3eaed693-68df-5da8-942d-408d6871358a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Real or Imaginary Part of a Scalar Given the Conjugate of a Scaled Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "5ec4fe6e-b357-5721-86d0-298df3fd33cf" :question/math-academy-id "e-7345" :question/problem "Find $\\textrm{Im}(k)$ given that\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\textrm{i} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$\\begin{bmatrix}8\\textrm{i} - 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$" :question/worked-solution "Since\n\n$$\n\\overline{k\\mathbf{v}} = \\overline{k} \\, \\overline{\\mathbf{v}}\n$$\n\nwe get the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nkv^(―) &= k^(―)v^(―) \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}8\\textrm{i} - 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} &= k^(―)\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\textrm{i} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}^(―) \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}8\\textrm{i} - 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} &= k^(―)\\begin{bmatrix}-4\\textrm{i}^(―) \\\\ 0^(―)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}8\\textrm{i} - 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} &= k^(―)\\begin{bmatrix}4\\textrm{i} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n\\begin{bmatrix}8\\textrm{i} - 12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} &= \\begin{bmatrix}4\\textrm{i}k^(―) \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain that\n\n$$\n4\\textrm{i}\\,\\overline{k} = 8\\textrm{i}-12 \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad \\overline{k}=\\dfrac{8\\textrm{i}-12}{4\\textrm i} = 2+3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nk=\\overline{2+3\\textrm{i}}=2-3\\textrm{i}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\textrm{Im}(k)=-3\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152512 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2b677c92-5390-5cd1-b1d3-b84d180c2b3e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a0096aee-63a3-53d9-b8f6-938dab3e5144" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 - 2\\textrm{i} \\\\ -5\\end